delete-system-properties(1) asadmin Utility Subcommands delete-system-properties(1)

NAME
       delete-system-properties - removes one or more system properties of
       the domain, configuration, cluster, or server instance

SYNOPSIS
           delete-system-properties [--help] [--target target_name ]
           property_name[:property_name]*

DESCRIPTION
       The delete-system-properties subcommand deletes one or more system
       properties of a domain, configuration, cluster, or server instance.
       Multiple property names are separated by colons (:). Make sure that
       the system properties are not referenced elsewhere in the
       configuration before deleting them.

       This subcommand is supported in remote mode only.

OPTIONS
       --help, -?
           Displays the help text for the subcommand.

       --target
           This option specifies the target on which you are deleting the
           system properties. The valid targets for this subcommand are
           instance, cluster, configuration, domain, and server. Server is
           the default option.

OPERANDS
       property_name[:property_name]*
           A colon-separated list of names of the system properties to
           remove.

EXAMPLES
       Example 1, Deleting a Single System Property
           This example deletes the system property named http-listener-port.

               asadmin> delete-system-properties http-listener-port
               System Properties [http-listener-port] deleted from target server. Make sure you check their references.
               Command delete-system-properties executed successfully.

       Example 2, Deleting Multiple System Properties
           This example deletes the system properties named http-listener-port
           and https-listener-port.

               asadmin> delete-system-properties http-listener-port:https-listener-port
               System Properties [http-listener-port, https-listener-port] deleted from target server. Make sure you check their references.
               Command delete-system-properties executed successfully.

EXIT STATUS
       0
           subcommand executed successfully

       1
           error in executing the subcommand

SEE ALSO
       delete-system-property(1), create-system-properties(1), list-system-properties(1)

